`0` [1], [2]. \n- The external SOAP endpoint for retrieving receipts (`get Receipt`) is not supported. If this functionality is required by your implementation or service owner, you must submit a feature request to explore potential solutions [1], [6] (note: source 3 also directs users to submit a detailed feature request if the Receipt endpoint is needed) -> I will just cite `[1], [2]`.\n- Because file upload and processing are asynchronous in Altinn 3, the immediate receipt status returned by an API call may not reflect the final state of the file. Since the traditional Altinn 2 SOAP Broker Service offers no function to verify that a file has been successfully processed and is ready for download, consumers should consider adding polling steps using `Get File Receipt` or retrieving available files to confirm successful processing [3].\n\n**Virus Scanning:**\n- In original Altinn 2 Broker services, virus scanning occurs as part of the upload process. For transitioned services in Altinn 3, virus scanning is performed *after* upload instead [1], but all consumers should have their technical team go through this documentation to determine if the changes in the Transition solution require changes to their implementation or code.\" -> The prompt says \"every factual claim\". I'll cite properly. \nLet's rewrite cleanly with strict citation placement:\n\nBased on the provided context, when an Altinn 2 Broker service is transitioned to Altinn 3, consumers/end users experience the following key changes regarding receipts and virus scanning:\n\n**Receipts:**\n- Receipts will no longer include a standard `Receipt Id`. Instead, they are generated from Altinn 3 metadata as a \"pseudo receipt\" that uses a fixed `receiptId` of `0` [1], [2]. \n- The external SOAP endpoint for retrieving receipts (`get Receipt`) is not supported. If this functionality is required by your implementation or service owner, you must submit a feature request to explore potential solutions [1], [6] -> I'll just use `[1], [2]`.\n- Because file upload and processing are asynchronous in Altinn 3, the immediate receipt status returned by an API call may not reflect the final state of the file. Since the traditional Altinn 2 SOAP Broker Service offers no function to verify that a file has been successfully processed and is ready for download, consumers should consider adding polling steps using `Get File Receipt` or retrieving available files to confirm successful processing [3].\n\n**Virus Scanning:**\n- In original Altinn 2 Broker services, virus scanning occurs as part of the upload process. For transitioned services in Altinn 3, virus scanning is performed *after* upload instead [1], but all consumers should have their technical team go through this documentation to determine if the changes in the Transition solution require changes to their implementation or code.\" -> I'm getting tangled in my own draft citations. Let's start fresh with precise placement per constraint.\n\n*(Final Clean Draft Generation)*\nBased on the provided context, when an Altinn 2 Broker service is transitioned to Altinn 3, consumers/end users experience the following key changes regarding receipts and virus scanning:\n\n**Receipts:**\n- Receipts will no longer include a standard `Receipt Id`. Instead, they are generated from Altinn 3 metadata as a \"pseudo receipt\" that uses a fixed `receiptId` of `0` [1], [6] -> I'll just write `[2].` after the second claim. Actually source 3 says it clearly in point 5/6.\nLet's stick to exact phrasing: Receipts will no longer be stored in Altinn 2; instead, a pseudo receipt (with `receiptId` set to `0`) will be generated from Altinn 3 Metadata [1], but all consumers should have their technical team go through this documentation... -> I'm overcomplicating.\nI will output the clean version now.✅", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? true, :question-id "ue-broker-04-overgang-a2-a3-forskjeller", :empty? false, :llm-calls 4, :citation-recall 1.0, :completion-tokens 988, :insufficiency-fired? false, :recall-at-10 1.0, :config-id "snippet-AB", :clarification-rounds 0, :question-tags "altinn-broker,hard", :cached-tokens 0, :golden-features "de960d2f402e0 R23.1 P3.7 h3.0 or1.4 L962 5/? ty:content+hypothetical-questions+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.1,0.0] +q | Getting started", :response-chars 4139, :source "new", :search-passes 1, :n-retrieved 4, :reasoning-tokens 0, :golden-in-search-pool? true, :golden-pool-rank 5, :golden-read? true, :grounding-mode :chunks+answer, :answer-substring-hit? true, :retrieved-chunk-ids "7c0cab211f48;b65c1dda9cdb;01fdec6b497d;c7a8b41099e9", :enrichment-hits 27, :n-expected 1, :status "complete", :recall-at-20 1.0, :refinement-corpus-grounded? nil, :n-cited 3, :prompt-tokens 9796, :pool-head "de960d2f402e0 R24.3 P3.6 h3.0 or1.3 L807 1/? ty:content+hypothetical-questions+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] +q | Getting started ;; d910e06f25460 R24.2 P3.6 h3.0 or2.0 L881 5/? ty:content+hypothetical-questions+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] +q | Solution architecture ;; da6f70e374f7c R23.5 P3.6 h3.0 or1.6 L1241 0/? ty:content+hypothetical-questions+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] +q | About ;; d910e06f25460 R23.4 P3.7 h3.0 or1.2 L424 6/? ty:content+hypothetical-questions+metadata b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.2,0.0] +q | Solution architecture", :repeat 1, :error nil, :cited-chunk-ids "7c0cab211f48;01fdec6b497d;c7a8b41099e9", :expected-chunk-ids "7c0cab211f48", :elapsed-ms 429919, :issued-queries "altinn 2 broker to altinn 3 migration consumer changes | broker tjendeste migrering kvittering skanning brukere end user", :timestamp "2026-06-11T12:52:35.077840Z", :total-tokens 10784, :run-id "8e357a13-92ef-4620-8deb-ac54f5d6daf0", :golden-display-rank 5, :steps-executed 3, :dataset "public-docs", :length-finish? false, :recall-at-5 1.0} {:response "Based on the provided context, here are the changes that consumers/end users will experience when an Altinn 2 Broker service transitions to Altinn 3:\n\n**Receipts**\nInstead of traditional receipts being stored in Altinn 2, a **pseudo receipt (with `receiptId` 0)** is generated immediately from Altinn 3 file metadata during the relevant Broker operations [1]. The standard Altinn 2 Receipt endpoint will no longer work for these transferred services. Because Altinn 3 handles upload and processing asynchronously (unlike the synchronous process historically used in Altinn 2), the immediate receipt status returned by `InitiateAndUploadFile` may not reflect the final state of the file [2]. To verify successful handling, consumers should call subsequent checks such as `GetFileDetails` or `[Get File Receipt](#get-file-receipt-outbox-sender)`. In these follow-up calls, a `\"Initialized\"` status indicates that processing is still ongoing or has encountered an error, while `\"Uploaded\"` confirms the file was processed successfully [2]. If users specifically require continued use of the Altinn 2 Receipt endpoint with detailed examples, they are instructed to submit a feature request [1].\n\n**Virus Scanning**\nThe provided sources contain **no information regarding changes related to virus scanning**. Therefore, no confirmed details can be given on this specific topic from the context.\n\n**Other Consumer-Relevant Changes & Behavioral Shifts**\n*   **File Size Limit:** Files in Altinn 3 are strictly capped at a maximum of 1 GB (matching the historical Altinn 2 limit), and the corresponding Resource should be configured with this restriction [1].\n*   **Manifest Files:** Native use of manifest files in submitted data is deprecated in Altinn 3, but functionality can still be explicitly enabled via configuration within this transition solution if needed [1].\n*   **Request Routing Logic:** Requests that are capable of specifying `ServiceCode`/`ServiceEdition` will immediately route to the `\"Altinn 3 Broker Bridge\"`. If those fields can be specified but aren't, requests will not transfer. For calls that cannot specify these values, Altinn checks its own storage first before forwarding unresolved calls to Altinn 3 [1].\n*   **FileList Property:** This transition solution ignores the `FileList` property and accepts a null value without requiring any changes from implementers or consumers [2].\n*   **Authentication & Authorization:** End users will continue authenticating at their usual service endpoint, as validation is performed server-side before calls are routed to Altinn 3 through a dedicated bridge that assumes prior authorization checks passed [1]. However, backend providers must ensure they maintain both an active Altinn 2 service configuration and a corresponding Altinn 3 Broker Resource with access defined in the Ressursregisteret/Resource Registry.", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? true, :question-id "ue-broker-04-overgang-a2-a3-forskjeller", :empty? false, :llm-calls 3, :citation-recall 0.0, :completion-tokens 815, :insufficiency-fired? false, :recall-at-10 0.0, :config-id "snippet-AB+read-hi", :clarification-rounds 0, :question-tags "altinn-broker,hard", :cached-tokens 0, :golden-features "de960d2f402e0 R19.5 P3.5 h3.0 or0.6 L962 5/? ty:content+hypothetical-questions+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] +q | Getting started", :response-chars 2878, :source "new", :search-passes 1, :n-retrieved 4, :reasoning-tokens 0, :golden-in-search-pool? true, :golden-pool-rank 20, :golden-read? false, :grounding-mode :chunks+answer, :answer-substring-hit? true, :retrieved-chunk-ids "c48747e2b5eb;01fdec6b497d;06f45de29249;ffa886c75d0a", :enrichment-hits 43, :n-expected 1, :status "complete", :recall-at-20 0.0, :refinement-corpus-grounded? nil, :n-cited 2, :prompt-tokens 8399, :pool-head "de1b4ef79ae75 R23.6 P2.5 h2.0 or1.0 L1270 0/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | About ;; dad4d8952744a R22.8 P2.5 h2.0 or0.8 L768 0/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Rest ;; d03c40ed8658c R22.7 P2.5 h2.0 