specification**) by opening your organization's specific Swagger URL in a web browser: `https://<org>.apps.<env>.altinn.no/<org>/<app>/swagger` [1].\n\nThe sources explicitly distinguish between two variants of the OpenAPI specification for Altinn 3 apps, and their scopes differ significantly regarding schema inclusion:\n- **Generic app API** / traditional auto-generated specification: Exposes all endpoints regardless of configuration, but intentionally contains no information about different data types or datamodel schemas [1][2]. This spec is available prior to v8.6 as well [2].\n- **App-specific API** / app-specific specification: Exposes a reduced, purposeful set of APIs relevant for end-user systems and includes references to the necessary schema definitions for your specific data models [1][3]. This variant became available starting from version 8.6 (or NuGet package v8.6.0) onward [1][2].\n\nTo view the complete app-specific OpenAPI specification with datamodel schemas, you must load the Swagger URL in a browser rather than downloading or consuming it as a static file, since the schema references are generated dynamically per application context within your environment [2]. \n\nPlease note that some APIs may intentionally fall outside of any OpenAPI specification; these are typically for internal use and subject to undocumented changes without notice [1].", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? true, :question-id "ue-api-06-app-openapi-swagger-spec", :empty? false, :llm-calls 4, :citation-recall 1.0, :completion-tokens 724, :insufficiency-fired? false, :recall-at-10 1.0, :config-id "snippet-AB", :clarification-rounds 0, :question-tags "altinn-3-general,hard", :cached-tokens 0, :golden-features "de2aa5b3e74ef R18.7 P2.6 h2.0 or1.4 L1107 0/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Spec", :response-chars 1481, :source "new", :search-passes 2, :n-retrieved 3, :reasoning-tokens 0, :golden-in-search-pool? true, :gol